{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.CellularDepthFiltration","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.CellularDepthFiltration","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Operations","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":37,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.odd_component_ne_zero_iff_of_intertwines_of_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.odd_component_ne_zero_iff_of_intertwines_of_parity","kind":"theorem","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L384-L406","doc":"**What \"`d_II = 3` on a chiral pair\" reduces to.** For odd `d`, the\ndepth-`d` component of `Φ (e i)` is nonzero iff it differs from that of\n`Φ (e (τ i))`. The right-hand side is a non-degeneracy condition that no\nhypothesis here supplies: it is the residual conjecture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.component_swap_of_intertwines_of_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.component_swap_of_intertwines_of_parity","kind":"theorem","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L376-L382","doc":"For a chiral pair, the depth-`d` components are related by `(-1)^d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.odd_component_eq_zero_of_intertwines_of_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.odd_component_eq_zero_of_intertwines_of_parity","kind":"theorem","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L358-L374","doc":"**Odd-depth vanishing for self-conjugate cells**, conditional on the\nmatching hypothesis `hmatch` and the parity hypothesis `hpar` (orientation\nreversal acts on the depth-`d` component by `(-1)^d`), with no 2-torsion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.realisation_swap_of_intertwines","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.realisation_swap_of_intertwines","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L351-L356","doc":"Chiral pair ⇒ orientation reversal swaps the two realisations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.realisation_even_of_intertwines","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.realisation_even_of_intertwines","kind":"theorem","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L343-L349","doc":"Self-conjugate cell ⇒ its realisation is orientation-even —\nconditional on the matching hypothesis `hmatch`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.rows_transpose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.rows_transpose","kind":"theorem","line":328,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L328-L331","doc":"Transposition swaps the number of rows and the length of the first row,\nso a \"number of rows\" filtration is not `#`-stable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.rows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.rows","kind":"def","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L325-L326","doc":"Number of rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.aDepth_add_transpose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.aDepth_add_transpose","kind":"theorem","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L320-L323","doc":"The `#`-symmetrised depth `a(μ) + a(μ')` is transpose-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.aDepth_transpose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.aDepth_transpose","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L312-L318","doc":"**Transposition exchanges `a` and `n`:** `a(μ') = n(μ)`. So `#`, which\nsends `e_μ` to `e_{μ'}`, sends the `a`-depth to the `n`-statistic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.nStat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.nStat","kind":"def","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L307-L310","doc":"The statistic `n(μ) = Σ_i (i-1) μ_i`, written as a sum over cells of the\nrow index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.aDepth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.aDepth","kind":"def","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L296-L305","doc":"**Cell depth (GB-depth, owner ruling 2026-11-16): Lusztig's `a`-function**\nof the two-sided Kazhdan–Lusztig cell of shape `μ`, in the labelling where the\none-row shape `(n)` is the index representation: `a(μ) = Σ_i C(μ_i, 2)`.\nWritten as a sum over cells: the cell `(i, j)` contributes its column index\n`j`, because row `i` contributes `0 + 1 + ⋯ + (μ_i - 1) = C(μ_i, 2)`.\nThe identification with the `a`-function is cited (Lusztig; Kazhdan–Lusztig\n1979) and checked exactly for `n ≤ 5`; here `aDepth` is the combinatorial\nstatistic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.maxHookDepth_transpose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.maxHookDepth_transpose","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L286-L294","doc":"**Max-hook depth is transpose-invariant.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.hookLength_transpose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.hookLength_transpose","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L280-L284","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.maxHookDepth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.maxHookDepth","kind":"def","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L274-L278","doc":"Maximal hook length. This is the statistic the corpus formerly called\n\"GB-depth\" (`gbDepth`); since the owner ruling of 2026-11-16 GB-depth is\nLusztig's `a`-function (`aDepth` below), so this one is renamed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.hookLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.hookLength","kind":"def","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L269-L272","doc":"Hook length of cell `c = (i, j)` (same definition as the corpus's\n`TwoFiltrationBridge.hookLength`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.map_gen_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.map_gen_add","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L255-L259","doc":"…and `e i + e (τ i)` is a `(+1)`-eigenvector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.map_gen_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.map_gen_sub","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L249-L253","doc":"For a chiral pair, `e i - e (τ i)` is a `(-1)`-eigenvector of `φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.map_gen_eq_self_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.map_gen_eq_self_iff","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L242-L247","doc":"`e i` is `φ`-fixed iff its cell is self-conjugate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.OrthIdem.injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.OrthIdem.injective","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L232-L240","doc":"Orthogonal nonzero idempotents are pairwise distinct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.map_F_stable_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.map_F_stable_iff","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L211-L230","doc":"**`#`-stability criterion.** For a `φ` permuting nonzero orthogonal\nidempotents by an involution `τ`, the filtration is `φ`-stable at every level\nif and only if the depth is `τ`-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.gen_mem_F_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.gen_mem_F_iff","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L201-L209","doc":"With nonzero orthogonal idempotents, a generator lies in `F k` exactly when\nits depth is at most `k`: the filtration determines the depth function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.map_F_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.map_F_eq","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L185-L199","doc":"**`#` transports the filtration, as an equality.** Under the hypotheses of\n`map_mem_F_comp`, the image of `F δ k` is exactly `F (δ ∘ τ) k`: the reverse\ninclusion holds because `e i = φ (e (τ i))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.map_mem_F_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.map_mem_F_comp","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L170-L183","doc":"**`#` transports the filtration.** If `φ` permutes the idempotents by an\ninvolution `τ`, then `φ (F δ k) ⊆ F (δ ∘ τ) k` for every depth `δ`. For the\n`a`-function this is the statement that `#` carries the `a`-filtration to the\nfiltration by `a ∘ transpose = n` (`aDepth_transpose`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:cellular-depth-filtration","label":"prop:cellular-depth-filtration","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.map_mem_F_of_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.map_mem_F_of_perm","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L157-L168","doc":"**`#` preserves the filtration** when it permutes the idempotents by a\ndepth-preserving `τ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.one_not_mem_F_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.one_not_mem_F_zero","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L140-L146","doc":"Corollary: if some depth is positive, `1 ∉ F 0`; the filtration is not a\nunital algebra filtration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.one_mem_F_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.one_mem_F_iff","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L126-L138","doc":"**The unit sits at the top.** With a complete family of nonzero\northogonal idempotents, `1 ∈ F k` iff every depth is `≤ k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.gen_mul_eq_zero_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.gen_mul_eq_zero_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L112-L124","doc":"An idempotent of depth `> k` annihilates `F k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.mul_mem_F_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.mul_mem_F_add","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L107-L110","doc":"In particular `F` is a multiplicative filtration in the usual sense. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.mul_mem_F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.mul_mem_F","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L98-L105","doc":"**Multiplicativity.** `F j * F k ⊆ F (min j k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.gen_mul_gen_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.gen_mul_gen_mem","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L89-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.gen_mem_F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.gen_mem_F","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L86-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.F_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.F_mono","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L83-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.F","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L77-L79","doc":"The cellular depth filtration `F δ k = span {e i | δ i ≤ k}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.OrthIdem.orth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.OrthIdem.orth","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.OrthIdem.idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.OrthIdem.idem","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.OrthIdem.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.OrthIdem.mk","kind":"ctor","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.OrthIdem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.CellularDepth.OrthIdem","kind":"structure","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cellular-depth-filtration.lean#L71-L74","doc":"A family of pairwise-orthogonal idempotents. ","signatureChunk":0}]}